Passes only if every one of these holds on that run (the forex scorecard; forex has no buy-and-hold, so the benchmark is holding nothing):
(1) Sharpe above zero after spreads and financing, and the profit still positive with 1.5% a year more markup (2.5% in all: profit minus 1.5 x the report's cost per 1% of markup);
(2) deflated Sharpe at least 95% against the forex pool;
(3) Sharpe above zero in at least half of the non-overlapping 2-year windows;
(4) the spread could be at least 2x what it was before the profit is gone;
(5) at least 30 trades, max drawdown no worse than -50%, and never wiped out.
Only if (1)-(5) all pass: (6) neighbouring settings, lookback 189 and 315 trading days (two more runs, two more trials), must both have a Sharpe above zero.

If all pass, it may go to the forex holdout (2023-01 onward) once, through its own frozen note, reported with and without EUR/USD and GBP/USD and passing both ways. If any fails, the note is rejected (with Luke's say-so). Run once; no setting changes after the result (a different lookback, volatility target, cap, or a carry signal would be a new note and new trials).
